DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggeettggrroouuppss() system call gets the current group access list of the
     user process and stores it in the array _g_i_d_s_e_t.  The _g_i_d_s_e_t_l_e_n argument
     indicates the number of entries that may be placed in _g_i_d_s_e_t.  The
     ggeettggrroouuppss() system call returns the actual number of groups returned in
     _g_i_d_s_e_t.  At least one and as many as {NGROUPS_MAX}+1 values may be re‐
     turned.  If _g_i_d_s_e_t_l_e_n is zero, ggeettggrroouuppss() returns the number of supple‐
     mentary group IDs associated with the calling process without modifying
     the array pointed to by _g_i_d_s_e_t.

     The value of {NGROUPS_MAX} should be obtained using sysconf(3) to avoid
     hard-coding it into the executable.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     A successful call returns the number of groups in the group set.  A value
     of -1 indicates that an error occurred, and the error code is stored in
     the global variable _e_r_r_n_o.

EERRRROORRSS
     The possible errors for ggeettggrroouuppss() are:

     [EINVAL]           The argument _g_i_d_s_e_t_l_e_n is smaller than the number of
                        groups in the group set.

     [EFAULT]           The argument _g_i_d_s_e_t specifies an invalid address.

